@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+# Bounded local TEST context
+
+The built-in compressor supports an explicit, text-only test policy on one named
+custom provider/model. Normal Hermes admission still requires 64,000 tokens; the
+existing explicitly pinned LM Studio exception is unchanged. This mode does not
+change advertised or served capacity, load a model, resize a server, or certify
+that a model can use tools reliably.
+
+## Profile configuration
+
+The following values illustrate a disposable test profile. Replace them with the
+actual serving limits and independently validated output/template reservations.
+They are **not defaults**. Use a literal loopback address or an RFC1918 IPv4 LAN
+address; hostnames and public addresses are rejected. The endpoint, named provider,
+model and Chat Completions transport must match on main and compression routes.
+
+```yaml
+model:
+  provider: custom:local-test
+  default: local-model
+  base_url: http://192.168.50.10:8001/v1
+  context_length: 40960
+providers:
+  local-test:
+    base_url: http://192.168.50.10:8001/v1
+    api_mode: chat_completions
+    # Configure this endpoint's existing credential through native provider config.
+    models:
+      local-model:
+        context_length: 40960
+        bounded_context:
+          mode: local_test
+          server_max_input_tokens: 40954
+          main_max_output_tokens: 4096
+          compression_max_output_tokens: 4096
+          safety_margin_tokens: 512
+          template_overhead_tokens: 1024
+fallback_providers: []
+auxiliary:
+  title_generation:
+    enabled: false
+  compression:
+    provider: custom:local-test
+    model: local-model
+    base_url: http://192.168.50.10:8001/v1
+    api_mode: chat_completions
+    context_length: 40960
+    fallback_chain: []
+    extra_body:
+      max_tokens: 4096
+compression:
+  enabled: true
+```
+
+All policy fields are required, with positive integer budgets. Unknown fields,
+boolean/string budgets, conflicting context pins, nonpositive usable input,
+external context engines and fallback chains are rejected. The compression cap is
+supplied through the existing `auxiliary.compression.extra_body` seam. Use exactly
+one verified output field, `max_tokens` or `max_completion_tokens`; contradictory
+SDK/extra-body caps and output increases beyond policy limits are rejected.
+Admitted test agents skip Ollama server autodetection; `model.ollama_num_ctx`
+overrides are rejected because this policy cannot resize the server context.
+
+Native runtime resolution may return `provider="custom"` while retaining
+`requested_provider="custom:local-test"`. Both identities are checked along with
+the actual request client's URL. No provider is relabelled as LM Studio.
+
+## Native invocation
+
+Load the profile using the existing profile mechanism. All surfaces that construct
+`AIAgent` use the same policy binding. When its `max_tokens` argument is omitted
+(`None`), the admitted policy's `main_max_output_tokens` supplies the main agent
+and compressor reservation. There is no new `agent.max_tokens` YAML setting.
+An explicit argument remains supported and must not exceed the policy maximum.
+For a native Python host using an already resolved runtime:
+
+```python
+agent = AIAgent(
+    model="local-model",
+    provider=runtime["provider"],             # native resolution may be "custom"
+    requested_provider="custom:local-test",
+    base_url=runtime["base_url"],
+    api_key=runtime["api_key"],
+    api_mode="chat_completions",
+    skip_context_files=True,
+    skip_memory=True,
+)
+```
+
+The first supported test scope is one model, fixed text tools and the compression
+auxiliary task. Other auxiliary tasks fail closed in this profile. Disable title
+generation and avoid features requiring vision, separate auxiliary models or
+fallback routes. This implementation is not acceptance of CLI/gateway, tool or
+provider configurations that have not been tested on the final profile.
+
+## Accounting and compression
+
+Each final Chat Completions request is checked after Relay/middleware changes;
+auxiliary progress streams, sync/async calls and internal parameter/credit retries
+also check at the SDK boundary. SDK `extra_body` precedence is included. The body
+accounts for system text once, user/assistant/tool messages, arguments, tool
+schemas and request-only fields. Multimodal content is outside the test scope.
+
+For the actual output reservation `O`, input budget is
+`min(server_max_input_tokens, context_length - O) - safety_margin_tokens`.
+The conservative estimate is the UTF-8 byte count of compact JSON plus the explicit
+template reserve. This is **not tokenizer-exact**, and a configured reserve is not
+a mathematical proof of chat-template fit. Accounting reports
+`tokenizer_verified: false`. Server tokenizer/template evidence and real provider
+usage comparisons remain mandatory before accepting a runtime profile.
+
+Preflight uses the same conservative byte units, independently of provider usage
+anchors. Its trigger is bounded at 75% of the smaller main/compression usable
+budget after template reserve; an existing lower `compression.threshold_tokens`
+cap is honored. Rough-estimate deferral is disabled only for this explicit mode.
+It does not forge a real usage anchor or disable cooldown, ownership, checkpoint,
+anti-thrash, attempt or compression-commit fences.
+
+Optional tail retention is limited to a conservative share of the available main
+budget. The TEST tail walk prices complete serialized rows in UTF-8 bytes too;
+using rough tokens here would retain several times the intended byte allowance
+and can leave a full native system/tool request over budget after compression.
+Automatic preflight notices label this pressure as conservative bytes plus the
+template reserve. Native newest-user and atomic tool-call/result anchors remain mandatory.
+The native algorithm is unchanged: prune within the transaction, choose boundaries,
+then make one summary call. Summary input reserves room for the full previous
+summary, instructions, bounded memory context, focus and output before sampling the
+eligible transcript. Sampling coverage remains observable. Summary output guidance,
+including its detailed log, fits the configured reservation. Empty, refused and
+length-truncated summaries still fail, preserving the original history.
+
+A protected head/tail or previous summary can itself be too large. Such a request
+may remain blocked after bounded compression attempts; it must not be dispatched
+or silently resized. Middleware/Relay additions that appear after early preflight
+are caught by the final guard; a late guard rejection does not invent another
+compression or retry loop.
+
+## Implementation seams
+
+`agent/bounded_context.py` owns immutable validation, admission, budgeting and
+physical guards. `SummaryInputMixin` in `agent/context_compressor_input.py` owns the
+existing sampling algorithm with a per-call input limit. Native constructor,
+request assembly and compressor consumers only bind or consult that policy.
+Related existing helpers were moved into `auxiliary_fallback_recovery.py` and
+`chat_completion_nonstream.py` to preserve the repository's file-size ratchet.
+Default routes retain their original budget and recovery behavior.
+
+Behavior checks live in `tests/agent/test_bounded_local_context.py` and run through
+`scripts/run_tests.sh`. SDK tests use owned in-process HTTP fixtures, including a
+real native turn → compression → post-compression dispatch sequence and a retained
+user-history case that stops without a main request. These tests prove wiring and
+negative controls; they do not prove local-model acceptance.
+
+`tests/agent/test_bounded_native_envelope.py` adds the complete native prompt
+builder, a Friday SOUL fixture, the native `session_search` schema and handler,
+and persisted history. Its SDK transport supplies a substantial summary and
+tool responses without network or inference. It checks post-compression physical
+request fit, protected user/tool failures, and raw history preservation under the
+explicit 40,960 context / 4,096 output / 1,024 margin / 2,048 template TEST profile.
